    "result_text": "The change is complete and the full suite is green (`BUILD SUCCESS`, `Tests run: 1, Failures: 0, Errors: 0`).\n\n## Summary\n\nI replaced the direct level rules with a points system that maps into a level, returning both fields.\n\n**`MembershipLevelAssigner`** (`rest/controller/`) \u2014 now tallies `membershipPoints` from the owner's standing and bands them into `membershipLevel`, keeping each concern in its own small method:\n- `points(owner)`: 0 base, `+2` email, `+1` when `namesakeCount == 0`, `+2` for household \u2265 3, `+3` for tenure > 365 days. Tenure is still `0` on create, so those points are never earned at creation (as before).\n- `levelForPoints(points)`: 1 (0\u20131), 2 (2\u20133), 3 (4\u20135), 4 (6+).\n- The thresholds/awards are named constants; the household check reuses the `householdSize` already assigned upstream, and the JavaDoc documents the new ordering requirement (after `NamesakeCounter` **and** `HouseholdSizeAssigner`).\n\n**`Owner`** model \u2014 added the `membership_points` column with `getMembershipPoints`/`setMembershipPoints` and refreshed both JavaDocs; MapStruct maps the new property to the DTO automatically by name.\n\n**`openapi.yml`** \u2014 added the read-only `membershipPoints` schema property and updated the `membershipLevel` description to reflect the banding rule (so both fields are exposed in the generated DTO/response).\n\n**DB schemas** \u2014 added `membership_points INTEGER` to all four `schema.sql` files (hsqldb/h2/postgres/mysql); the hsqldb one is what the test profile uses with `ddl-auto=none`.\n\nThe acceptance test confirms a fresh owner with an email and no namesakes scores `membershipPoints=3` \u2192 `membershipLevel=2`.",
