    "probe_text": "Here is the complete, ordered sequence for `POST /api/owners` \u2014 the `addOwner` handler in `OwnerRestControllerV1` (`src/main/java/.../rest/controller/v1/OwnerRestControllerV1.java:183`). Nothing else in the codebase maps that route (the V2 controller only exposes a paged `GET`).\n\n## Phase 0 \u2014 before the method body runs\n\n**Security gate**\n1. `@PreAuthorize(\"hasRole(@roles.OWNER_ADMIN)\")` \u2014 caller must have the `OWNER_ADMIN` role, else 403.\n\n**`@Valid @RequestBody` on `OwnerFieldsDto`** (bean-validation constraints from the generated DTO):\n2. `firstName` \u2014 `@NotNull`, `@Pattern` (letters, 1\u20133 space/`'`/`-`-separated words), `@Size(1..30)`.\n3. `lastName` \u2014 `@NotNull`, `@Pattern` (same, trailing `.` allowed), `@Size(1..30)`.\n4. `address` \u2014 `@NotNull`, `@Size(1..255)`.\n5. `city` \u2014 `@NotNull`, `@Size(1..80)`.\n6. `telephone` \u2014 `@NotNull`, `@Size(1..20)`.\n7. `postcode` \u2014 `@Size(max 255)` (optional).\n\n**Registered `@InitBinder` validators** (run as part of the same `@Valid` pass \u2014 see `initOwnerFieldsBinder`, line 151):\n\n`OwnerFieldsValidator` (in this order):\n8. **Normalizes `address`** to canonical form and writes it back onto the DTO (side-effect \u2014 happens even before the emptiness checks).\n9. Requires non-blank: `firstName`, `lastName`, `address`, `city`, `telephone`.\n10. If `telephone` had no prior error: **normalizes it to E.164** and writes it back; rejects if not a valid number.\n11. `email` (optional): must be syntactically valid, must **not** be on the disposable-domain blocklist, and on success is **normalized to lowercase** and written back.\n12. `postcode` (optional): must be a valid 4-digit code for the owner's `city`.\n\n`RegistrationDateValidator`:\n13. If `registrationDate` is supplied, it must not be after the server's current date (no future registration).\n\nAny failure in phase 0 produces a **400 Bad Request** and the method body never runs.\n\n## Phase 1 \u2014 method body (executed top-to-bottom)\n\n14. `ownerMapper.toOwner(...)` \u2014 maps the (now-normalized) DTO to an `Owner` entity.\n15. `registrationDateAssigner.assign` \u2014 **side-effect:** sets the registration date, defaulting to today's date when none was supplied, then rolls a Saturday/Sunday forward to the next business-day Monday.\n16. `cityCapacityChecker.isCityAtCapacity` \u2014 **validation:** if the city already holds \u2265 50 owners \u2192 **409 Conflict**, abort.\n17. `dailyRegistrationLimiter.isDailyLimitReached(registrationDate)` \u2014 **validation:** if \u2265 100 owners already carry that (adjusted) registration date \u2192 **429 Too Many Requests**, abort.\n18. `householdAssigner.assign` \u2014 **side-effect:** sets `householdId`, derived deterministically from last name + postcode.\n19. Reads the DTO's `sharesHousehold` flag.\n20. `householdDuplicateChecker.isDuplicate` \u2014 **validation:** if another owner shares the household (same last name + postcode) **and** `sharesHousehold` is not true \u2192 **409 Conflict**, abort.\n21. `identityDuplicateChecker.isDuplicate` \u2014 **validation:** if an existing owner has the same identity key (telephone + email + householdId) \u2192 **409 Conflict**, abort.\n22. Computes `declaredHouseholdMember = householdDuplicate && sharesHousehold`.\n23. `householdSizeAssigner.assign` \u2014 **side-effect:** sets `householdSize` (stored household members + 1).\n24. `customerCodeAssigner.assign` \u2014 **side-effect:** sets `customerCode` as `<REGION>-<HASH8>` (region from postcode/city; hash of normalized telephone + last name).\n25. `namesakeCounter.assign` \u2014 **side-effect:** sets `namesakeCount` (existing owners with same first+last name, case-insensitive).\n26. `membershipLevelAssigner.assign` \u2014 **side-effect:** sets `membershipPoints` and the banded `membershipLevel` (email, no-namesake, large-household points; tenure points always 0 on create).\n27. `bulkSignupWarningAssigner.assign` \u2014 **side-effect:** sets `bulkSignupWarning` = true when > 80 owners already share the registration date.\n28. `possibleDuplicateAssigner.assign(owner, declaredHouseholdMember)` \u2014 **side-effect:** sets `possibleDuplicate` and `possibleDuplicateOf`; skipped (left unflagged) for a declared household member.\n29. `clinicService.saveOwner(owner)` \u2014 **side-effect:** persists the owner (assigns its id).\n30. `ownerCreationAuditLogger.logCreated(owner)` \u2014 **side-effect:** writes an audit line to the `AUDIT` logger (id, customerCode, registrationDate, membershipLevel).\n31. Builds the response: maps to `OwnerDto`, sets the `Location: /api/owners/{id}` header, returns **201 Created**.\n\nA couple of things worth flagging: the DTO-mutating steps in phase 0 (address canonicalization, telephone E.164 rewrite, email lowercasing) are *validation-time side-effects* \u2014 the stored/returned values are the normalized forms. And the several count-based checks (capacity, daily limit, household/identity duplicates, namesakes, household size) all run against the current store *before* the save, so they never count the new owner itself."
